WEBVTT

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.404
Whoa!

00:00:22.492 --> 00:00:23.618
Stay close.

00:00:36.297 --> 00:00:37.840
What happened here?

00:00:44.138 --> 00:00:45.139
[growls]

00:00:45.223 --> 00:00:46.224
All right, easy, bud.

00:00:46.307 --> 00:00:47.684
[gasps] Hiccup!

00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:49.310
[man] Fire!

00:00:49.477 --> 00:00:50.520
Astrid, look out!

00:00:52.355 --> 00:00:53.398
[grunting]

00:00:54.232 --> 00:00:55.400
Hiccup!

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:58.611
[all shouting]

00:01:00.405 --> 00:01:02.532
Watch the tail! [grunts]

00:01:03.491 --> 00:01:05.243
Tie those legs up!

00:01:07.078 --> 00:01:08.288
Huh?

00:01:08.621 --> 00:01:09.789
Is that what I think it is?

00:01:09.914 --> 00:01:10.915
[Hiccup] Stop!

00:01:11.124 --> 00:01:12.584
[Astrid] Stormfly!

00:01:13.793 --> 00:01:15.211
What are you doing?

00:01:16.546 --> 00:01:17.589
[trappers] Whoa!

00:01:17.672 --> 00:01:18.756
Back again?

00:01:20.383 --> 00:01:22.468
Soil my britches.

00:01:22.635 --> 00:01:25.138
That is a Night Fury.

00:01:25.346 --> 00:01:27.432
I thought they were all gone for good.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.184
It looks like our luck's
had a turn for the better, lads.

00:01:30.393 --> 00:01:32.937
Don't think Drago has one of those

00:01:33.146 --> 00:01:34.272
in his dragon army.

00:01:34.439 --> 00:01:35.899
Dragon army?

00:01:36.065 --> 00:01:37.734
Look, we don't want any trouble.

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:38.985
Ha!

00:01:39.068 --> 00:01:40.778
You should have thought of that

00:01:40.862 --> 00:01:42.488
before you stole all of our dragons,

00:01:42.697 --> 00:01:44.824
and blasted our fort to bits!

00:01:44.908 --> 00:01:46.743
[trappers talking indistinctly]

00:01:46.826 --> 00:01:48.161
What are you talking about?

00:01:48.328 --> 00:01:50.038
You think we did this?

00:01:50.496 --> 00:01:53.458
[scoffs] Dragon trapping
is hard enough work

00:01:53.541 --> 00:01:56.002
as it is without do-gooder dragon riders

00:01:56.169 --> 00:01:57.754
sneaking in to rescue them.

00:01:57.962 --> 00:01:59.672
What do-gooder?

00:02:00.506 --> 00:02:02.675
There are other dragon riders?

00:02:02.967 --> 00:02:06.262
You mean other than your thieving friend
from last night? You tell me.

00:02:06.346 --> 00:02:09.682
You may have
an ice-spitting dragon on your side,

00:02:09.766 --> 00:02:11.684
but we still have a quota to fill.

00:02:11.851 --> 00:02:14.979
How do you suppose we explain
this mess to Drago Bludvist?

00:02:15.104 --> 00:02:18.608
Drago what-fist?
Does anything you say make sense?

00:02:18.775 --> 00:02:22.737
He's expecting a new shipment of
dragons for his army by tomorrow.

00:02:22.904 --> 00:02:26.240
And Drago don't take well to excuses.

00:02:26.449 --> 00:02:28.117
This is what he gave me

00:02:28.242 --> 00:02:30.536
last time I showed up empty-handed.

00:02:30.703 --> 00:02:34.165
He promised to be
far less understanding in the future.

00:02:34.832 --> 00:02:37.377
All right, look, we don't know
anything about a dragon thief

00:02:37.543 --> 00:02:38.920
or an ice-spitting dragon

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:43.257
or your lunatic boss
and his dragon army, okay?

00:02:43.424 --> 00:02:46.219
Just give us back our dragon and we'll go,

00:02:46.386 --> 00:02:49.013
strange, hostile person
whom we've never met.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:51.057
Oh, where are my manners? [chuckles]

00:02:51.599 --> 00:02:52.600
I'm Eret,

00:02:53.017 --> 00:02:54.644
son of Eret.

00:02:55.395 --> 00:02:57.939
Finest dragon trapper alive.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:00.233
After all,

00:03:00.316 --> 00:03:03.277
it's not just
anyone who can capture a Night Fury.

00:03:03.361 --> 00:03:04.779
[snarls]

00:03:04.862 --> 00:03:07.824
This is Toothless.
He says we're going. Now.

00:03:07.907 --> 00:03:09.409
[laughs]

00:03:09.575 --> 00:03:10.868
They all say that.

00:03:10.952 --> 00:03:11.953
Rush 'em, lads!

00:03:12.036 --> 00:03:13.037
[trappers shouting]

00:03:13.705 --> 00:03:15.081
[trappers exclaiming fearfully]

00:03:19.168 --> 00:03:20.169
Stormfly! Come on!

00:03:20.378 --> 00:03:21.379
Go! Go!

00:03:25.758 --> 00:03:28.177
You will never hold on to those dragons,

00:03:28.344 --> 00:03:29.595
you hear me?

00:03:29.762 --> 00:03:32.390
Drago is coming for them all!

00:03:35.393 --> 00:03:37.395
-[Fishlegs] Come on, Meatlug!
-[Tuffnut] Whoo-hoo!

00:03:37.478 --> 00:03:38.646
[Ruffnut] Yahoo!

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:40.148
[dragons chittering]

00:03:40.898 --> 00:03:42.483
-[Snotlout] Whoa!
-[gasps]

00:03:43.067 --> 00:03:44.152
[grunts]

00:03:44.235 --> 00:03:45.695
[all laughing]

00:03:47.321 --> 00:03:48.364
[man] Hey, there, Stoick!

00:03:48.448 --> 00:03:49.866
Hey, how are you? Beautiful day.

00:03:49.949 --> 00:03:51.159
Hello, Spitelout. Great race.

00:03:51.242 --> 00:03:52.326
[Spitelout grumbles]

00:03:52.493 --> 00:03:54.037
Oh, sorry, Mrs. Ack.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.163
Any sign of him?

00:03:55.246 --> 00:03:58.458
Ah! He's probably flown off
the edge of the world by now.

00:03:58.583 --> 00:04:00.793
Are you sure you want
that kid running the village?

00:04:00.877 --> 00:04:03.171
You can still delay your retirement.

00:04:03.337 --> 00:04:04.589
He's ready. You'll see.

00:04:04.672 --> 00:04:05.923
[dragons screech]

00:04:06.507 --> 00:04:09.052
[laughs] There he is! Huh?

00:04:09.927 --> 00:04:12.513
The pride of Berk!

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:15.683
Who finally decided
to show up for work. Yay.

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:17.477
Sorry. Got held up.

00:04:17.643 --> 00:04:18.853
Hey, Dad, could I have a word?

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:21.064
Something you're itching to tell me?

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:23.816
Not quite the itch
you're thinking of, but yes.

00:04:23.983 --> 00:04:26.861
Good man! Now, lesson one.

00:04:27.028 --> 00:04:30.114
A chief's first duty
is to his people, so, 41?

00:04:30.281 --> 00:04:32.325
-Can we just talk in private?
-Forty…

00:04:32.492 --> 00:04:34.702
That's me! That's me! I'm next!

00:04:34.869 --> 00:04:36.162
If we could just talk…

00:04:36.329 --> 00:04:38.164
Excuse me. I have been here all day.

00:04:38.331 --> 00:04:40.792
Okay, okay.
I want one of those high seaters

00:04:40.958 --> 00:04:44.295
with lots of spikes
and a big stowage compartment.

00:04:44.462 --> 00:04:46.380
Absolutely. You got it, sir.

00:04:46.547 --> 00:04:49.425
This is actually a little more important
than building saddles.

00:04:49.509 --> 00:04:51.636
Lesson two. No task is too small

00:04:51.719 --> 00:04:53.596
when it comes to serving your people.

00:04:53.763 --> 00:04:55.264
Excuse us, Grump.

00:04:55.348 --> 00:04:56.349
Dad, can we just talk…

00:04:56.516 --> 00:04:57.683
[Gobber] Grump!

00:04:57.850 --> 00:04:59.769
You let the forge die down again!

00:05:01.813 --> 00:05:03.022
[all gasp]

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:08.694
[Gobber] That's it, Grump.
You're going up for adoption.

00:05:08.945 --> 00:05:11.322
There you go. Go on. Have away.

00:05:11.781 --> 00:05:13.908
Seriously, I really need to tell you

00:05:13.991 --> 00:05:16.035
about this new land we came across.

00:05:16.202 --> 00:05:17.870
-Another one?
-Any new dragons?

00:05:18.037 --> 00:05:19.872
We didn't stick around to find out.

00:05:20.039 --> 00:05:23.000
These folks weren't particularly friendly.

00:05:23.084 --> 00:05:26.003
Oh, really? Your Night
Fury and Deadly Nadder

00:05:26.087 --> 00:05:27.922
didn't bring them
cheering to the rooftops?

00:05:28.089 --> 00:05:29.549
No, this was different.

00:05:29.757 --> 00:05:32.885
Not the standard run-for-the-hills
hoo-ha I've come to enjoy.

00:05:33.052 --> 00:05:35.555
These guys were trappers.

00:05:36.013 --> 00:05:37.557
Dragon trappers.

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:39.016
You should have seen their fort.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:43.271
All blown apart and stuck in
giant spikes of ice. It was weird!

00:05:43.437 --> 00:05:45.356
I've never seen anything like it.

00:05:45.523 --> 00:05:47.567
And worst of all, they thought we did it!

00:05:47.733 --> 00:05:49.777
You two are gonna get yourselves

00:05:49.861 --> 00:05:51.904
in serious trouble one of these days.

00:05:52.113 --> 00:05:54.782
Not everyone appreciates this way of life.

00:05:55.241 --> 00:05:56.576
Aye, Gobber's right, son.

00:05:56.742 --> 00:05:57.994
Best we keep to our own.

00:05:58.119 --> 00:06:01.122
Besides, you'll have
more important uses for your time.

00:06:01.581 --> 00:06:03.124
[chuckles]

00:06:03.249 --> 00:06:05.751
Once we make the big announcement!

00:06:06.711 --> 00:06:09.213
They are building a dragon army.

00:06:10.756 --> 00:06:13.676
Or at least the guy they work for is.

00:06:14.093 --> 00:06:16.721
Dargo Bloody Fist, or something.

00:06:18.931 --> 00:06:22.685
I'll bloody his fist with my face
if he tries to take my dragon!

00:06:22.852 --> 00:06:23.853
Or mine!

00:06:24.103 --> 00:06:25.521
[groans] You're such a moron.

00:06:25.688 --> 00:06:26.814
A beautiful moron.

00:06:26.898 --> 00:06:28.191
-Yeah.
-[groans]

00:06:28.733 --> 00:06:31.485
Bludvist? Drago Bludvist?

00:06:31.611 --> 00:06:33.321
Yeah. Wait.

00:06:33.821 --> 00:06:34.989
You know him?

00:06:38.034 --> 00:06:39.035
Ground all dragons!

00:06:39.118 --> 00:06:40.119
[Hiccup] What? Why?

00:06:40.203 --> 00:06:41.579
[Stoick] Seal the gates!

00:06:41.871 --> 00:06:43.164
Lower the storm doors!

00:06:43.247 --> 00:06:44.415
Wait! What is happening?

00:06:44.498 --> 00:06:45.499
[Gobber] Come on!

00:06:45.583 --> 00:06:46.918
You heard the man! Lock it down.

